1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,822
Your solar plant is covered in shit.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:04,048
Literally.

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:07,203
But how much is that affecting production?

4
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:10,930
That is the question behind PoopVolt.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,370
An older solar plant still works.

6
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:19,032
But its owner cannot tell
whether it produces

7
00:00:19,282 --> 00:00:21,082
as much as it should.

8
00:00:21,332 --> 00:00:24,905
The maintenance company
needs clear evidence

9
00:00:25,155 --> 00:00:29,330
to explain why an inspection
is worth considering.

10
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,813
PoopVolt compares observed production

11
00:00:33,063 --> 00:00:35,928
with an expected reference
over the same period.

12
00:00:36,178 --> 00:00:39,124
Today, we have a comparison
between inverters.

13
00:00:39,374 --> 00:00:43,475
A theoretical reference adjusted
for environmental conditions

14
00:00:43,725 --> 00:00:44,995
is the next step.

15
00:00:45,245 --> 00:00:48,037
A deviation tells us where to investigate,

16
00:00:48,287 --> 00:00:49,500
not what caused it.

17
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:53,530
The prototype uses Arduino UNO Q

18
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:57,731
with temperature, humidity,
light, a display, and NFC.

19
00:00:57,981 --> 00:01:00,835
The schematic also shows
the current sensor

20
00:01:01,085 --> 00:01:03,806
between the panel and the charging system.

21
00:01:04,055 --> 00:01:06,006
Zero current has been checked;

22
00:01:06,256 --> 00:01:09,252
measurements under light
still need validation.

23
00:01:09,502 --> 00:01:11,842
The board runs on USB power,

24
00:01:12,092 --> 00:01:13,990
separate from the solar branch.

25
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,356
In a replay of SOLARMA’s historical data,

26
00:01:18,522 --> 00:01:20,437
we compare 13 inverters.

27
00:01:20,602 --> 00:01:24,048
From 1 August to 17 September 2019,

28
00:01:24,213 --> 00:01:26,662
inverter 1 reports zero energy

29
00:01:26,827 --> 00:01:30,157
against roughly 292 kWh

30
00:01:30,322 --> 00:01:31,974
expected from its peers.

31
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:34,226
The software flags it for inspection.

32
00:01:34,391 --> 00:01:36,245
This is historical replay,

33
00:01:36,410 --> 00:01:39,500
not our panel’s measurement
or a soiling diagnosis.

34
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,948
The technician investigates and proposes

35
00:01:42,948 --> 00:01:45,552
cleaning, repair,
or replacement where needed.

36
00:01:45,552 --> 00:01:46,808
The owner decides.

37
00:01:46,808 --> 00:01:50,213
Afterward, comparable measurements
must verify the benefit;

38
00:01:50,213 --> 00:01:52,350
the full gap may not be recoverable.

39
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:54,018
PoopVolt turns a production gap

40
00:01:54,018 --> 00:01:56,500
into an understandable
intervention proposal.
